From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 27 Aug 2026 12:37:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: expose QCA8386 PHY serial modes

QCA8386 integrates the four-port QCA8084 PHY package.  The QCA8084 PHY
driver advertises SGMII for 10/100/1000 links and 2500BASE-X for 2.5G.
Expose both modes on QCA8386 user ports so phylink can intersect the
switch and PHY interface capabilities when the ports use PHY handles.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -1537,6 +1537,12 @@ static void qca8k_phylink_get_caps(struc
 			  config->supported_interfaces);
 		__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_INTERNAL,
 			  config->supported_interfaces);
+		if (qca8k_is_qca8386(priv)) {
+			__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII,
+				  config->supported_interfaces);
+			__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX,
+				  config->supported_interfaces);
+		}
 		break;
 
 	case 6: /* 2nd CPU port / external PHY */
